% python go.py --index
index:
  app 1 needs web 2..3, db 1..2
  app 2 needs web 3, db 2
  web 1 needs http 1
  web 2 needs http 1..2
  web 3 needs http 2
  db 1
  db 2 needs http 1
  http 1
  http 2
  cli 1 needs web 1
roots: app 1..2
plan: app 1, web 3, http 2, db 1
[[package]]
name = "app"
version = 1
dependencies = ["web 3", "db 1"]

[[package]]
name = "db"
version = 1

[[package]]
name = "http"
version = 2

[[package]]
name = "web"
version = 3
dependencies = ["http 2"]

% python go.py app=2
roots: app 2
no plan
a plan exists without any one of these requirements:
  app 2 needs web 3
  app 2 needs db 2
  web 3 needs http 2
  db 2 needs http 1
every branch of the search ends in a conflict:
  app 2 > db 2 needs http 1, but app 2 > web 3 picked http 2
exit status 1
% python go.py --yank web=3
roots: app 1..2
yanked: web 3
plan: app 1, web 2, http 2, db 1
[[package]]
name = "app"
version = 1
dependencies = ["web 2", "db 1"]

[[package]]
name = "db"
version = 1

[[package]]
name = "http"
version = 2

[[package]]
name = "web"
version = 2
dependencies = ["http 2"]

% python go.py --lock plan.lock
roots: app 1..2
locked: app 1, db 2, http 1, web 2
plan: app 1, web 2, http 1, db 2
[[package]]
name = "app"
version = 1
dependencies = ["web 2", "db 2"]

[[package]]
name = "db"
version = 2
dependencies = ["http 1"]

[[package]]
name = "http"
version = 1

[[package]]
name = "web"
version = 2
dependencies = ["http 1"]

% python go.py app=1 cli=1
roots: app 1, cli 1
no plan
a plan exists without any one of these requirements:
  the root app 1
  the root cli 1
  app 1 needs web 2..3
  cli 1 needs web 1
every branch of the search ends in a conflict:
  app 1 > db 2 needs http 1, but app 1 > web 2 picked http 2
  app 1 > db 2 needs http 1, but app 1 > web 3 picked http 2
  cli 1 needs web 1, but app 1 picked web 2
  cli 1 needs web 1, but app 1 picked web 3
exit status 1
% python go.py app=5
roots: app 5
no plan
every branch of the search ends in a conflict:
  the roots need app 5, and the index has no such version
exit status 1
% python go.py tls=1
roots: tls 1
no such package: tls
exit status 2
